    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "formule",
     "title": "The wave equation",
     "md": "**v = f × λ** (speed in m/s, frequency in Hz, wavelength in m). Speed depends on the medium; frequency is set by the source. Waves can be **reflected**, **refracted** (change of speed gives a change of direction) and **diffracted** (spread round obstacles and through gaps, most when the gap is about one wavelength). These can be shown in a **ripple tank**."
