   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "key",
     "style": "definition",
     "title": "Sound",
     "md": "Sound is made by **vibrating** objects and travels as a **longitudinal wave** of compressions and rarefactions. It needs a **medium** (solid, liquid or gas) and **cannot travel through a vacuum**. Approximate speeds: **air about 340 m/s**, water about 1500 m/s, steel about 5000 m/s: it is fastest in solids. Humans hear frequencies from about **20 Hz to 20 000 Hz**; above 20 000 Hz is **ultrasound**."
